# Katon — environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# RULE (locked decision #5): secret/service keys are SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix a
# secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that exposes it in the client bundle.

# --- Supabase (server-only) ---
# Service role key bypasses RLS; it must stay server-side.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Payments ---
# Unset means CLOSED: no new payments, and `POST /api/pay` answers 503
# `payment_closed`. That is the production value and it is deliberate.
# `mock` walks the paid flow for free and is Preview/local ONLY - it is refused
# whenever VERCEL_ENV=production, because it is a free unlock.
# `doku` ARRIVED IN PROMPT V (2026-09-21) and is the real provider. Nothing else is
# a value; anything else reads closed, including a stale `xendit`.
PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=

# --- DOKU Checkout (QRIS) ---
# Server-only. NEVER prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Back Office -> Integrations -> API keys. The SECRET both signs outbound requests
# and verifies inbound notifications, which makes it the one value in this file that
# must never reach a log line.
#
# BOTH OR NEITHER. With `doku` selected and one missing, the fence refuses with a
# named reason - `doku_client_id_unset` or `doku_secret_key_unset`, separate because
# they are two different mistakes in two different Vercel fields - rather than
# quietly reading as an open shop.
DOKU_CLIENT_ID=
DOKU_SECRET_KEY=

# PRESENT = api-sandbox.doku.com. ABSENT = api.doku.com.
#
# REFUSED IN PRODUCTION, and this is the subtler of the two free-unlock fences. A
# sandbox key in production is not "take money", it is "pretend to": the checkout
# page looks real, the buyer pays, DOKU sends a genuinely signed notification, the
# row flips to paid, and no money has moved. Every guard downstream passes, because
# each one is working correctly on a test transaction. Nothing but the fence in
# lib/paymentFence.js can tell the difference.
DOKU_SANDBOX=

# TEMPORARY, and it should not outlive Prompt V. Set it in PREVIEW ONLY to make
# /api/doku/notify print the four headers and the raw body of a VERIFIED notification,
# which is how the walk captures the fixture V-doku.md section 4 requires. Fenced three
# ways: this flag, never under VERCEL_ENV=production, and only AFTER the HMAC passes -
# the rule it sits beside is "the reason, never the body", and that rule is about an
# UNVERIFIED body, which anyone can POST. The secret is never printed.
# It comes out in its own commit once the fixture lands. See the DEFERRED REGISTER.
DOKU_CAPTURE=

# XENDIT_SECRET_KEY and XENDIT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN are GONE (2026-09-18). Reyner ruled the
# exit outright and lib/xendit.js is deleted, so nothing reads them. UNSET THEM IN
# VERCEL - this file has twice recorded a variable that stayed set after its code
# went away, and one of those became the architecture. Closing the ACCOUNT is a
# separate act and it is Reyner's: the 2026-10-01 fee is on the account, not on
# whether a key is still typed into a project.

# --- App ---
# Used to build the share link katon.app/r/<token>.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://katon.app

# MIRROR_PREVIEW_TOKEN is GONE (2026-08-23), and this note replaces it for the same
# reason the NEXT_PUBLIC_FREE_FULL_READING note below exists: a deleted variable
# left in a deploy is a variable someone will assume still does something.
#
# It was QA access to /api/mirror while that route was linked from nowhere - unset
# meant the route 404'd entirely, sent as an `x-mirror-preview-token` header rather
# than a query parameter. PROMOTION removed the requirement, which is exactly what
# this variable's own note said would happen, and lib/mirror/fence.js went with it.
# The funnel front door creates and reads mirror readings now.
#
# UNSET IT IN VERCEL. It is inert - no code reads it - but leaving a stale secret in
# a project's environment is how NEXT_PUBLIC_FREE_FULL_READING became architecture.
# Nothing replaces it: the mirror is the product, its ceiling is the rate limiter,
# and the paywall is `row.paid === true` in lib/deliver/handlers.js.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_FREE_FULL_READING is GONE (2026-08-05). It ungated the full reading
# for cafe tests, was left set in Vercel, and became the de facto architecture: the
# paywall never rendered in production and Xendit rejected the site for having no
# checkout. Deleted with lib/flags.js. Do not reintroduce it as an env var.

# ── THE RENDERER HAS ONE PROVIDER (CLAUDE.md rule 15) ──────
# Gemini, with module assembly as the failover. Ruled by Reyner 2026-08-22; the OpenAI
# secondary was deleted in the same commit. It had never run: arming it needed a model
# id no document in this repo ever named, so `openaiConfigured` returned false for the
# project's whole life and the chain skipped it every time.
#
# THE CONSEQUENCE IS OPERATIONAL, NOT ARCHITECTURAL. With no second provider, a Gemini
# outage or an exhausted balance is a 100% floor rate - every reader gets module
# assembly. The mitigation is a balance alert on the Gemini account, which does not
# exist yet and is in the deferred register.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
